# Two slices sharing one backing array, and what an append does to it.
Shot slice
Alt a slice and a reslice of it, :slice drawing both over the one backing array they share, then an append through the reslice that overwrites an element of the original
Caption :slice draws the backing array two slices share — so the append that quietly overwrites x[3] is something you can see coming.
Headline See the backing array
Promo 16:9
Grid 80x26
Line x := []int{1, 2, 3, 4, 5}
Line y := x[1:3]
Line :slice x, y
Line y = append(y, 99)
